Hi,

I hope this type of solicitation for request of experts on this mailing list
is ok – I apologize in advance if I am violating any terms of use….

My company is looking to outsource the development of laptop PC software
that can be used to transmit special sequences of WiFi test signals that we
can use for our R&D and testing of our wireless beamforming algorithms. 

The software will need to periodically send bursts of WiFi packets at
different RF center frequencies in the 5-6 GHz frequency bands. The time
between bursts, number of packets per burst, time between packets, RF center
frequencies of the transmitted packets will be user-configurable through a
command-line-interface, but typically there will be one burst per second,
and 20 packets per burst with each packet being sent at a different
frequency and with an inter-packet spacing of 10 milliseconds. 

We are open to the choice of laptop, OS and WiFi card that are used to
develop the software, but our preference is to use Windows XP SP3 or Ubuntu
Linux, using an Atheros-based WiFi card - details provided in a requirements
spec we've written that we can make available. 

